## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical detection pipeline for cloud-native DNS tunneling, combining kernel telemetry, DNS-layer analytics, and service-mesh visibility; emphasizes real-world validation and false-positive control.

## Key Concepts
- eBPF DNS egress monitoring
- CoreDNS analytics and entropy-based signals
- Istio telemetry integration and namespace scoping
- Multi-signal alerting and validation
- Synthetic traffic to verify detections

## Code Example
```javascript
function entropy(s){
  const counts = {};
  for(const ch of s) counts[ch]=(counts[ch]||0)+1;
  const total = s.length;
  let e=0; for(const c of Object.values(counts)){ const p=c/total; e -= p*Math.log2(p); }
  return e;
}
function isSuspicious(domain){
  const parts = domain.split('.');
  const labels = parts.slice(0,-1);
  const ent = labels.map(l=>entropy(l)).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  const len = domain.length;
  return ent>3.5 || len>30;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune thresholds to reduce false positives across tenants?
- What data retention and RBAC would you implement for CoreDNS and eBPF telemetry?

## Why This Is Asked

Introduces a practical policy gate that enforces manifest hygiene early in CI, ensuring traceability and consistency across deployments.

## Key Concepts

- YAML manifest traversal and metadata fields
- Distinguishing annotations vs labels and required keys
- Lightweight Node.js validator using js-yaml
- Integrating validator into GitHub Actions as a PR gate

## Code Example

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const yaml = require('js-yaml');
function valid(manifest) {
  const m = yaml.load(fs.readFileSync(manifest, 'utf8'));
  const meta = m?.metadata || {};
  const ann = meta.annotations || {};
  const lab = meta.labels || {};
  return ann['app.kubernetes.io/managed-by'] === 'ci-tool' && lab.app && lab.version;
}
module.exports = { valid };
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend the validator to report which manifests fail and why?
- How would you adapt the workflow to run in parallel across multiple directories?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply attestation to WASM plugins in edge/k8s environments, a realistic gap beyond container images.

## Key Concepts

- WASM module signing with cosign
- Rekor attestations for wasm artifacts
- Runtime verification in a restricted loader
- Policy enforcement with Kyverno/OPA
- Edge CI/CD integration with registry labels

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo loader verification
async function verifyAndLoad(wasmName) {
  const att = await fetch(`https://rekor.example/attestations/${wasmName}`);
  if (!att?.valid) throw new Error('Attestation missing or invalid');
  // Load WASM module
  return await WebAssembly.instantiateStreaming(fetch(wasmName));
}
```
